In Java 8, the double colon (::) operator is called method references.
This is implementation of abstract method of functional interfaces,it means instead of implementing lambda expression implementation,use already implemented one
There are four kinds of method references:

Reference to a static method ClassName::staticMethodName
Reference to an instance method of a particular object Object::instanceMethodName
Reference to an instance method of an arbitrary object of a particular type ContainingType::methodName–
Reference to a constructor ClassName::new